1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,928
My voice is gone forever, and tomorrow the whole city will finally scream my name.

2
00:00:06,228 --> 00:00:14,100
Seven days ago, a sleek broker offered me eternal fame if I signed away every spoken word.

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,352
I laughed, but my guitar had stayed silent for years. Hunger makes a man trade his soul.

4
00:00:20,652 --> 00:00:29,292
I pressed my thumb on the glass. The contract vanished, and pure electricity flooded my fingertips instantly.

5
00:00:29,592 --> 00:00:37,608
Tonight, I step onto the biggest stage in London. Thousands wait in absolute, breathless anticipation.

6
00:00:37,908 --> 00:00:44,532
I strum a single chord. The sound shatters the night air, heavy and rich beyond belief.

7
00:00:44,832 --> 00:00:53,736
The crowd erupts into a deafening roar. Thousands of fans surge forward, chanting my name over and over.

8
00:00:54,036 --> 00:00:59,484
I smile and try to shout thank you, but no sound comes out of my open mouth.

9
00:00:59,784 --> 00:01:06,984
Then I look closer at the front row. Every single person is screaming, but their mouths remain completely closed.

10
00:01:07,284 --> 00:01:12,612
They gave up their voices for this too. Who are you really applauding for when no one can speak?
